.255.0'}]]": 1,
    "['unit [unit_number] encapsulation [encapsulation_type]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1\\n encapsulation dot1Q 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command sets VLAN bridging encapsulation for a logical unit (unit 1) with VLAN ID 10\\n- In Cisco, we create a subinterface (GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1) and use 802.1Q encapsulation with the VLAN ID\\n- Note that while the Juniper configuration separates the VLAN ID setting (in the next command), Cisco combines both the encapsulation type and VLAN ID in the encapsulation command\\n- The IP address assignment would be configured separately in Cisco, just like in Juniper\", 'trans_template': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'encapsulation dot1Q 10', 'parent_command': ['interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1'], 'root': 'interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Juniper configuration:\\n\\n##\\ninterface GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1\\n encapsulation dot1Q 10\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- The Juniper command sets VLAN bridging encapsulation for a logical unit (unit 1) with VLAN ID 10\\n- In Cisco, we create a subinterface (GigabitEthernet1/0/0.1) and use 802.1Q encapsulation with the VLAN ID\\n- Note that while the Juniper configuration separates the VLAN ID setting (in the next command), Cisco combines both the encapsulation type and VLAN ID in the encapsulation command\\n- The IP address assignment would be configured separately in Cisco, just like in Juniper\", 'trans_template': 'encapsulation dot1Q 10'}]]": 1,
